WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.980
- Thousands of police departments

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.240
use K9's to keep us safe.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.770
These highly-trained dogs work

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.990
alongside law enforcement
and are often sent

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:10.570
into extremely dangerous situations.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.890
But many lack the protection they deserve.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.590
That's where a 10-year-old boy from Ohio

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.230
has stepped up and has already raised

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:22.230
more than $130,000 to buy
bulletproof vests for dogs.

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:25.781
Please welcome Brady and
his momma Leah ya'll.

00:00:25.781 --> 00:00:29.030
(crowd cheering)

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.910
- So, so Brady, Leah, how did this start?

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.300
- I was watching this
show called Live P.D.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.581
And there was this K9
that didn't have a vest

00:00:36.581 --> 00:00:38.790
so I wanted to vest him.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:40.941
- Yeah I love that that's
such a sweet heart.

00:00:40.941 --> 00:00:43.660
- Yeah he was 8 years old at the time

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.510
and his stepdad's a police officer

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.491
so he knows the importance
of the Kevlar vest.

00:00:48.491 --> 00:00:51.380
I didn't even pick up that
the dog wasn't wearing one.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.687
He turned to me and was like,

00:00:52.687 --> 00:00:53.680
"What's going on?"

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.300
and to this day, that's when
he started Brady's K9 Fund

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.860
and he's raised over $130,000

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:01.020
and how many have you vested?

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:01.853
How many dogs?

00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:03.101
- 127

00:01:03.101 --> 00:01:04.670
- That is so cool, man!

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:05.941
(applause)

00:01:05.941 --> 00:01:07.590
That is so cool.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.010
So let's talk about the vest.

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:11.370
There are, these vests are
custom-made for the K9s

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.480
and they don't get, like, overheated,

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:13.690
they're specifically, kind of, for them?

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.870
- Yes, it's a whole new techology

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.050
that they're rolling out.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:19.920
They're protective of
just their vital organs,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.650
allows them have full movement,

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:22.800
which is super important.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:23.633
- Yeah.

00:01:23.633 --> 00:01:27.070
- And police departments rely on donations

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:28.555
for these vests because
they can't afford it.

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:29.550
- Yeah, it's not in the budget.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.610
- Yeah, the budget for K9s is really low.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:32.495
- It's like being a teacher.

00:01:32.495 --> 00:01:33.335
- Right?

00:01:33.335 --> 00:01:34.168
They have like no supplies, yeah, yeah.

00:01:34.168 --> 00:01:35.020
- It's like there's no budget.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.140
Yeah, yeah, agreed agreed.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.560
So you recently received a
big honor as well, right?

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.900
- Yeah so um, ASPCA told me

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.507
that I'm the Kid of the Year.

00:01:44.507 --> 00:01:45.498
(applause)

00:01:45.498 --> 00:01:47.219
- You got Kid of the Year?

00:01:47.219 --> 00:01:48.469
That's amazing!

00:01:49.848 --> 00:01:51.849
How did you feel receiving that?

00:01:51.849 --> 00:01:55.270
- Um, I was proud that they um picked me.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:57.660
- Yeah that's so cool, it's 'cause you're,

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.810
Dude, what were ya'll
doin' at nine and ten?

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:00.772
I wasn't savin' the world.

00:02:00.772 --> 00:02:01.605
- Not at all.

00:02:01.605 --> 00:02:02.438
- When I was eight I was,

00:02:02.438 --> 00:02:04.819
I was eating paint chips off the wall.

00:02:04.819 --> 00:02:06.650
(laughter)

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.760
- Like, I don't know if
I did anything that cool.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.070
That is, you've got such a big heart.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:11.903
I have-

00:02:11.903 --> 00:02:12.736
- Kid of the Year is crazy I,

00:02:12.736 --> 00:02:15.720
I don't even know that existed
to be a kid of the year.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:16.612
That's huge, brother.

00:02:16.612 --> 00:02:17.445
- Yeah

00:02:17.445 --> 00:02:18.278
- I know!

00:02:18.278 --> 00:02:19.111
And we didn't know it exists

00:02:19.111 --> 00:02:20.230
because we we weren't offered that.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:22.859
(laughter)

00:02:22.859 --> 00:02:24.950
The most recent recipient of a vest

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.410
from Brady's K9 fund is Mido

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.100
from the Hawthorne Police Department

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.300
here in California.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.370
He's here actually with his
handler, Officer Sarah Lewis.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:34.609
Ya'll come on out!

00:02:34.609 --> 00:02:37.537
(applause)

00:02:37.537 --> 00:02:38.931
Hi, nice to see you!

00:02:38.931 --> 00:02:39.764
- Hi.

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:41.983
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:41.983 --> 00:02:42.816
- And this is Mido

00:02:42.816 --> 00:02:44.850
- So, so you might wanna
keep Mido over here

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.867
because he's allergic to dogs.

00:02:46.867 --> 00:02:47.883
- Okay, oh no!

00:02:48.846 --> 00:02:49.679
- I'm not gonna die.

00:02:49.679 --> 00:02:50.512
- You wanna sit with me here?

00:02:50.512 --> 00:02:51.345
Why don't you take my seat?

00:02:51.345 --> 00:02:52.178
- No I...

00:02:52.178 --> 00:02:53.260
- I'll scoot down I'll sit by Brady.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.177
- Okay, well Mido's the star.

00:02:55.177 --> 00:02:56.010
- I don't want him to start like,

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:57.160
you know, getting in hives,

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.910
I want him to come back to my show.

00:02:59.985 --> 00:03:02.640
- So how will this vest make a difference?

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.380
- I mean I wear a vest, from here,

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.250
to protect my vital organs, so.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.750
Um, this is, this is amazing

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.860
and this vest in particular is really nice

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:12.770
because it's lighter weight so the dogs,

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.710
I, I can put this on Mido and keep him

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:17.150
in my car and because you never know,

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:18.675
sometimes if I contact a suspect.

00:03:18.675 --> 00:03:19.508
- Be quick

00:03:19.508 --> 00:03:20.810
- And they run and they're armed

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.190
I, I have a door pop right here

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.780
on my belt and I can pop him out.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.070
He's already got his protection on,

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:26.920
ready to go and I feel better about it

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.090
and he's safe.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.945
- Wow, it's so, look what you did, Brady!

00:03:29.945 --> 00:03:31.124
(applause)

00:03:31.124 --> 00:03:32.540
- That's so cool!

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.170
- Uh, this week the Cirque Dreams

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.830
kicked off their annual Holidaze show

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.840
coming to nearly 60 cities
from coast to coast.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.660
Here to tell us about this year's tour,

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:43.500
please welcome Broadway producer and

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.604
Cirque Dreams founder, Neil Goldberg!

00:03:45.604 --> 00:03:47.854
(applause)

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.654
So I, I love annual traditions

00:03:51.654 --> 00:03:54.140
and this one, this was, it's become one

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:55.040
'cause it's so huge.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:55.898
- It has!

00:03:55.898 --> 00:03:57.390
It's in it's twelfth year, 60 cities,

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.890
I mean this show has
something in it for everyone

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:02.065
and that's why people
keep going back to see it.

00:04:02.065 --> 00:04:02.898
- Yeah.

00:04:02.898 --> 00:04:04.254
- And all over the United States,

00:04:04.254 --> 00:04:05.260
you know, you can see it in the

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.710
fabulous Fox theaters in Atlanta

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:11.150
and, and in St. Louis, from Denver,

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.125
Philadelphia, Charlotte,
Connecticut, all over.

00:04:13.125 --> 00:04:14.100
- I love that you're
getting everywhere, yeah.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.580
- Yeah, everywhere and we keep going back

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.620
because it's a great tradition

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.190
because, you know, I grew up in New York

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.620
and my mom and dad used
to take us into the city

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.800
to see the Radio City
Christmas Spectacular

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:23.990
and what I remember as a kid was

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:26.310
that amazing feeling of mom and dad

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.030
taking the kids and the grandparents

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.030
and going to see something
about the holidays

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.700
that everyone can share.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:32.957
- And it almost like kicks
off the season for you.

00:04:32.957 --> 00:04:35.040
It's gets you in like
the spirit of everything.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:35.873
I love it.

00:04:35.873 --> 00:04:37.200
- It does and you know I also love

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.420
when people walk out of the theater

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.157
and sometimes I'll meet them
in the lobby and I'll say

00:04:40.157 --> 00:04:41.690
"So how did you think about the show?"

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:42.705
and they go, "I just want to go out

00:04:42.705 --> 00:04:44.320
and start shopping."

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:45.153
- [Kelly] Oh yeah.

00:04:45.153 --> 00:04:45.986
- And the show, you know,

00:04:45.986 --> 00:04:47.270
you hear the word "Cirque" so yeah

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:48.990
there's all that amazing acrobatic

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:51.020
audacity and trapeze and flying

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.990
But this is about the holiday season.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:55.640
Everyone of the twenty
scenes in this two hour show

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:56.830
tell another story.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:59.310
Penguins, North Pole, snowing, skiing.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.143
- Oh my gosh.

00:05:00.143 --> 00:05:01.660
- Toy soldiers walking on thin wire

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.890
so we've taken all of these amazing things

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:05.710
that people have seen
in these Cirque shows

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.006
in Vegas and on television

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:09.090
and we've themed them for the holidays

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:09.923
so this is great

00:05:09.923 --> 00:05:10.810
- And you're bringing them to the masses

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.060
and it's for families, like,

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:13.810
it's not just for adults, like,

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:14.720
it's everybody can come.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:15.553
That's what I love about it.

00:05:15.553 --> 00:05:16.841
- It is, it is, the adult worry about,

00:05:16.841 --> 00:05:17.880
you know, parking.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.561
We worry about stroller parking, so.

00:05:19.561 --> 00:05:21.110
(laughter)

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:23.010
- But Neil brought some of his performers

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.350
who are ready to give us a show.

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:25.473
Let's see it!

00:05:25.473 --> 00:05:26.306
(applause)

00:05:26.306 --> 00:05:28.889
(circus music)

00:05:46.404 --> 00:05:48.654
(applause)

00:05:51.793 --> 00:05:54.376
(crowd cheers)

00:06:11.543 --> 00:06:13.793
(applause)

00:06:22.164 --> 00:06:24.747
(crowd cheers)

00:06:29.997 --> 00:06:32.247
(applause)

00:07:16.238 --> 00:07:19.405
(cheers and applause)

00:07:21.055 --> 00:07:21.888
- What!?

00:07:23.415 --> 00:07:26.121
That was so incredible!

00:07:26.121 --> 00:07:26.954
- Thank you

00:07:26.954 --> 00:07:27.787
- Oh my gosh!

00:07:27.787 --> 00:07:28.620
- Thank you so much

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:31.064
- I thought for sure one was gonna drop.

00:07:31.064 --> 00:07:33.324
I mean, I, your skill is flawless.

00:07:33.324 --> 00:07:34.524
- That is what make us superior.

00:07:34.524 --> 00:07:35.357
- I'm like

00:07:35.357 --> 00:07:36.530
- That's like, that's like
you hitting a bad note.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:37.562
- I do.

00:07:37.562 --> 00:07:38.395
- We don't want that.

00:07:38.395 --> 00:07:39.280
- You just keep going.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:40.830
You'll impress 'em later.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.410
Um, you have something special though,

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:43.840
for Brady and Leah, right?

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:46.050
- I do, um, I'm personally, for,

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:47.450
on behalf of Cirque Dreams,

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:49.700
we are so proud of what
you have done, and,

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:52.082
like we said, the show
is playing in 60 cities,

00:07:52.082 --> 00:07:55.591
But our biggest show is
going to be in Colorado

00:07:55.591 --> 00:07:57.410
and everyone at Cirque Dreams

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.720
wanted me to represent to you

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:01.040
and your mom and dad that you're going

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.832
to come and see that show.

00:08:02.832 --> 00:08:03.665
- Yeah!

00:08:05.598 --> 00:08:06.431
- Yay!

00:08:06.431 --> 00:08:09.180
- I mean I would come
just for the juggling

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:11.190
and the dancing polar bear.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.023
That's amazing.

00:08:12.023 --> 00:08:14.810
Cirque Dreams Holidaze
is performing 60 shows

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:18.160
at the brand new Gaylord
Rockies Resort in Colorado

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.300
and the hotel is flying
Brady and his parents

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:24.430
to the resort where they'll
attend a performance as VIPs.

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:27.130
But that's not all, Cirque Dreams Holidaze

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:29.090
is also performing here
at the Dolby Theater

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:31.250
in Los Angeles and everyone in my audience

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:32.083
is getting tickets!

00:08:32.083 --> 00:08:33.696
(cheers and applause)

00:08:33.696 --> 00:08:34.928
And listen to this!

00:08:34.928 --> 00:08:36.968
Those tickets are good for any performance

00:08:36.968 --> 00:08:39.791
of Cirque Dreams Holidaze
around the country.

